# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalclearonly).
#
# One draw, three answers in the same boot:
#
#   1. a pass that only clears, read back before anything is drawn -- 1 means the clear action
#      reaches attachment 2 (RGBA32Uint), 0 means the render target's write path does not;
#   2. RWA_PRINT_NIR=1, the NIR of the fragment stage as it is handed to the driver, which says
#      whether clearFragment20's store is uint (bits kept) or int (which a Mali blend unit
#      writing a uint attachment saturates to 0);
#   3. the draw itself, and the pixel it leaves.
#
# v11's clear-to-1 read back 0 after the draw, which could be a shader writing zeros over it or
# a clear that never happened; 1 and 2 tell them apart.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props show
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props on
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --env RWA_PRINT_NIR=1 --draw --fragment clearFragment20 /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props off
